  "headline": "Supreme Court Orders Karthigai Deepam Lighting In Thiruparankundram",
  "seoTitle": "Karthigai Deepam Lighting In Thiruparankundram Supreme Court",
  "metaDescription": "The Supreme Court ordered the Karthigai Deepam to be lit at the Deepathoon pillar, leading to CRPF deployment and contempt notices for state officials.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The Supreme Court mandated the lighting of a ceremonial lamp at the Deepathoon stone pillar in Madurai, following past non-compliance issues.",
    "CRPF personnel have been deployed to secure the site, while state officials and the temple trust face contempt notices from the court.",
    "The Tamil Nadu government has filed a review petition, while political parties have expressed conflicting views on the judicial intervention."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The dispute centers on the location for lighting the Karthigai Deepam at the Thiruparankundram temple site. Following concerns over previous compliance, the Supreme Court issued a directive for the lamp to be illuminated at the Deepathoon stone pillar. To ensure this is carried out, the court authorized the deployment of Central Reserve Police Force (CRPF) personnel and suspended the existing temple trust. The directive also included the issuance of contempt notices to 15 state bureaucrats. The Tamil Nadu government has subsequently filed a review petition to challenge the court's interim order. The situation has elicited reactions from various political figures, with the Bharatiya Janata Party welcoming the court's stance and local Congress leadership calling for a judicial review regarding the implications for temple administration and federal governance principles.",
